;;; Syntax probe — wrappers.
;;;
;;; The three S1.7c.4 wrapper heads as what they are now: ordinary fact
;;; heads with nested facts as arguments.
;;;
;;; One of the eighteen node-kind fixtures. As corpus entries they are
;;; rendered under every parse view and every op, and each rendering is
;;; digested by `corpus_shapes.md5`, so a change to how any of these
;;; shapes is drawn moves a digest. They exist because no *puzzle*
;;; contains these shapes.
;;;
;;; A nested fact takes no keyword (Q-M1e2.28, S1f.5.11's default), so the
;;; inner facts carry none. Until M1f S1f.5.5's T1f.5.5.10 (2026-11-08) they
;;; carried `:source "(1)"` and `:rule sym :using (x)`, which the loader
;;; dropped, so no stored fact moved when they went (Q-M1f.2 (a)).

(ontology (relation r T T) (is-a a T))
(facts (r a b))
(reasoning (r b c))
